  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Several chances for rain this weekend into \nnext week. \n\nEarly this evening, waves of patchy light rain and drizzle \ncontinue to cross the region. Through the overnight, additional\nshort wave energy will keep the rain going. On Saturday, \nanother short wave pushes through and will bring scattered \nshowers and maybe an isolated thunderstorm mainly to points \nalong and east of the Blue Ridge. To the west, drier air will be\nslowly filtering in and will limit rainfall. \n\nOn Sunday and Monday, convection looks limited again with drier\nair in place, so most folks should see a break. NW flow aloft \nbrings another round of energy through late Monday night into \nTuesday, with a strong cold front moving through sometime late \nTuesday into early Wednesday. After that, we should get another \nbreak from daily rain chances for at least a couple days. \n\nWe are outlooked for both a 15% chance of severe weather from\nSPC on Day 5 (Tuesday), as well as a Marginal Risk of excessive \nrainfall from WPC with the cold frontal passage. UCAR's medium \nrange convective model is also highlighting Tuesday for a severe\nweather threat, which would consist of damaging winds and heavy\nrain possibly leading to flash flooding.\n\nWe should see a gradual warm up over the weekend. Temperatures \nreach the low 80s for most mountain locations by Monday, and mid\nto upper 80s for the Piedmont and Roanoke regions. Even a few \nlow 90s are possible early next week in gusty WSW surface flow \nfor Roanoke and the Piedmont areas.",
